# python slice: the RPC arm (design/SHAPES.md)
# interpreter:  3.11.15 (main, Mar  3 2026, 09:26:23) [GCC 13.3.0]
# grpcio:       1.84.0
# payload:      P2.2, 540422 bytes, decoded at the CLIENT
# server:       returns pre-serialised bytes and never encodes, so both arms
#               share it and only the response_deserializer differs
# grid:         A = upb codec + grpcio transport (the incumbent, end to end)
#               B = upb codec + CORE transport   -> B - A is the TRANSPORT
#               C = core codec + core transport  -> C - B is the CODEC
# transport:    ArmoniK INTENDS 2097152 B chunking and a 4194304 B window; it SHIPS
#               neither -- no ArmoniK client pins an HTTP/2 window today -- so
#               the stack-default row is the shipped configuration.
# headline:     CPU per RPC. Wall clock is beside it because R9's hazard moves
#               wall clock and does not move CPU
# allocator:    pinned, as in bench.py (applied)

