## Nagle: is a small response dearer than a large one?
   transport       bytes       ms/RPC
   unix             1024        0.688
   unix           540422        1.149
   tcp              1024        0.688
   tcp            540422        1.123
   Monotone in size on both transports, with nothing near 40 ms, means the C
   core sets TCP_NODELAY itself. The artifact was the tonic SERVER's under
   serve_with_incoming and it does not reach a Python caller -- and there is no
   grpc.tcp_nodelay in this build, so it is not a setting anyone could have got
   wrong from here.

